  "_comment": "2 long jobs (single 150.0s op) arrive at t=0 on Weld[1]; starting at t=5.0, 40 short jobs (~12.0s) stream in every 5.0s on the SAME machine -- arrival rate (1/5.0) exceeds single-machine service rate for short jobs alone (1/12.0), so the queue never empties for the whole 200s stream. Under SPT the long jobs never look shortest and starve for the whole stream; under FIFO they ran first at t=0 and never starve. Look at job IDs 0..1's individual flow-time, not the mean/p95 -- they're outnumbered 40:2 so aggregate stats can dilute the effect.",
